To clarify this, since there was confusion recently in another thread,
you must first break the statue, then step on the pile to see if a
spellbook is buried beneath (the rocks are always on top, thus you see
the rocks only... *).

The spellbook is NOT UNDER the unbroken statue, as several people
thought I was implying when I said that I move around the statues in
the Oracle room before breaking them... it's much easier to do with a
wand or spell if they all get broken at once :)

For a statue to contain a spellbook, it must not be of a tiny monster,
and pass the random chance rn2(level_difficulty()/2 + 10) > 10, where
level difficulty is equal to the dungeon level if you do not have the
amulet of yendor, equal to the deepest level you have reached if you
have the amulet (ie, the sanctum level) but are not in the planes, and
equal to the sanctum's DL + 1/2 your XL if in the endgame.

This check being integer math means that you can never find a book
inside a statue on DL 1 and 2.  Spellbooks are only generated when the
statue is generated (ie, level creation) which means that waiting to
break the statue after you have the amulet is pointless.  Also, any
statues that you make (with a method of stoning) will contain only the
inventory the monster started with, never a random spellbook (unless,
of course, the monster was already carrying a spellbook).

